 "notes": ["Incumbent Maura Healey (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Massachusetts' governor's race features incumbent Democrat Maura Healey seeking a second term against Republican Mike Minogue, with independent Andrea James also on the ballot. Every public poll this fall has shown Healey leading by at least 16 points, and the most recent surveys from Suffolk University and UMass Amherst put her margin in the low-to-mid 20s. The state's strong Democratic lean and Healey's incumbency reinforce that picture.\n\nMinogue has campaigned on cost-of-living issues and challenged Healey's honesty, and a pro-Minogue super PAC has been active, but coverage suggests his Trump ties weigh more heavily with this electorate. Betting markets price Healey's chances at 96 to 98 percent, and every major race rater labels the contest Solid or Safe Democratic. The open question is the size of Healey's victory margin, not who wins.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9961, "margin": 18.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9947, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9921, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9953, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9924, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9932, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9949, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9959, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9955, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.996,